      "sensitivity": "non-sensitive",
      "aiSeverity": null,
      "aiValidity": null,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `transferFrom()` function in TokenWrapper emits a `Transfer` event with `msg.sender` (the spender) as the `from` address instead of the actual token owner whose balance is being debited. This violates the ERC20 standard and causes incorrect event data to be emitted.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\nIn [TokenWrapper.sol:127-155](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/TokenWrapper.sol#L127-L155), the `transferFrom` function correctly updates balances but emits an incorrect Transfer event:\n\n```solidity\nfunction transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n    uint256 allowanceCurrent = allowance[from][msg.sender];\n    if (allowanceCurrent != type(uint256).max) {\n        if (allowanceCurrent < amount) revert InsufficientAllowance();\n        unchecked {\n            allowance[from][msg.sender] = allowanceCurrent - amount;\n        }\n    }\n\n    uint256 balance = _balanceOf[from];\n    if (balance < amount) {\n        revert InsufficientBalance();\n    }\n    unchecked {\n        _balanceOf[from] = balance - amount;  // Correctly debits 'from'\n    }\n\n    if (to == address(CORE)) {\n        coreBalance += amount;\n    } else {\n        _balanceOf[to] += amount;  // Correctly credits 'to'\n    }\n    emit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);  // BUG: Should be Transfer(from, to, amount)\n    return true;\n}\n```\n\nThe issue is on line 153: `emit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount)` emits the spender's address instead of the token owner's address (`from`).\n\n### Root Cause\n\nCopy-paste error or oversight - the Transfer event parameter should be `from` (the token owner) not `msg.sender` (the spender).\n\n\n## Impact\n\nThis bug violates the ERC20 standard (EIP-20) which specifies that Transfer events MUST emit the actual token owner as the `from` address. The impact includes:\n\n1. Off-chain indexer corruption: Services tracking token balances via Transfer events (The Graph, Dune Analytics, custom indexers) will have completely incorrect balance data. As demonstrated in the POC, an indexer would show:\n   - Token owners appearing to never lose tokens (balance never decreases)\n   - Spenders appearing to have negative balances (impossible state)\n\n2. Block explorer incorrect data: Etherscan, Blockscout, and other explorers will display incorrect transfer history showing the wrong sender\n\n3. DeFi integration failures: Protocols relying on Transfer events for:\n   - Balance reconciliation\n   - Transaction history\n   - Accounting and auditing\n   - Tax reporting tools\n\n4. Wallet tracking issues: Wallets that use event logs to track token movements will show incorrect transaction history\n\n- It does not result in direct loss of funds (balances are correctly updated on-chain)\n- However, it causes significant integration issues and data corruption for any system relying on ERC20 Transfer events\n- The TokenWrapper is designed to be used as a standard ERC20 token, so correct event emission is critical for ecosystem compatibility\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\nChange line 153 in TokenWrapper.sol from:\n\n```solidity\nemit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);\n```\n\nTo:\n\n```solidity\nemit Transfer(from, to, amount);\n```\n\nThis single-line fix ensures the Transfer event correctly identifies the actual token owner as the sender, bringing the contract into ERC20 compliance.",
      "proofOfConcept": "Save this POC in `test/poc/M03_TokenWrapperIncorrectTransferEvent.t.sol`\n\nRun the POC:\n```bash\nforge t --mp test/poc/M03_TokenWrapperIncorrectTransferEvent.t.sol -vv\n```\n\n\n### POC Code\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test, Vm} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"forge-std/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"../FullTest.sol\";\nimport {TokenWrapper} from \"../../src/TokenWrapper.sol\";\nimport {TokenWrapperFactory} from \"../../src/TokenWrapperFactory.sol\";\nimport {TestToken} from \"../TestToken.sol\";\nimport {BaseLocker} from \"../../src/base/BaseLocker.sol\";\nimport {ICore} from \"../../src/interfaces/ICore.sol\";\nimport {FlashAccountantLib} from \"../../src/libraries/FlashAccountantLib.sol\";\n\ncontract TokenWrapperPeripheryForPOC is BaseLocker {\n    using FlashAccountantLib for *;\n\n    constructor(ICore core) BaseLocker(core) {}\n\n    function wrap(TokenWrapper wrapper, address recipient, uint128 amount) external {\n        lock(abi.encode(wrapper, msg.sender, recipient, int256(uint256(amount))));\n    }\n\n    function handleLockData(uint256, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory) {\n        (TokenWrapper wrapper, address payer, address recipient, int256 amount) =\n            abi.decode(data, (TokenWrapper, address, address, int256));\n\n        ACCOUNTANT.forward(address(wrapper), abi.encode(amount));\n        if (uint128(uint256(amount)) > 0) {\n            ACCOUNTANT.withdraw(address(wrapper), recipient, uint128(uint256(amount)));\n        }\n        if (uint256(amount) != 0) {\n            ACCOUNTANT.payFrom(payer, address(wrapper.UNDERLYING_TOKEN()), uint256(amount));\n        }\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\ncontract M03_TokenWrapperIncorrectTransferEventTest is FullTest {\n    TokenWrapperFactory factory;\n    TokenWrapperPeripheryForPOC periphery;\n    TestToken underlying;\n    TokenWrapper wrapper;\n\n    address alice;\n    address bob;\n    address charlie;\n\n    event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint256 value);\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        FullTest.setUp();\n        underlying = new TestToken(address(this));\n        factory = new TokenWrapperFactory(core);\n        periphery = new TokenWrapperPeripheryForPOC(core);\n        wrapper = factory.deployWrapper(IERC20(address(underlying)), 0);\n\n        alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n        bob = makeAddr(\"bob\");\n        charlie = makeAddr(\"charlie\");\n\n        underlying.transfer(alice, 1000 ether);\n    }\n\n    function test_M03_POC_TransferFromEmitsWrongFromAddress() public {\n        uint256 wrapAmount = 100 ether;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), wrapAmount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, alice, uint128(wrapAmount));\n\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), wrapAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(bob, 50 ether);\n\n        vm.recordLogs();\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, charlie, 50 ether);\n\n        Vm.Log[] memory logs = vm.getRecordedLogs();\n\n        bytes32 transferEventSig = keccak256(\"Transfer(address,address,uint256)\");\n\n        bool foundTransferEvent = false;\n        address emittedFrom;\n        address emittedTo;\n        uint256 emittedAmount;\n\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < logs.length; i++) {\n            if (logs[i].topics[0] == transferEventSig && logs[i].emitter == address(wrapper)) {\n                foundTransferEvent = true;\n                emittedFrom = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[1])));\n                emittedTo = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[2])));\n                emittedAmount = abi.decode(logs[i].data, (uint256));\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        assertTrue(foundTransferEvent);\n        assertEq(emittedTo, charlie);\n        assertEq(emittedAmount, 50 ether);\n\n        assertEq(emittedFrom, bob);\n        assertTrue(emittedFrom != alice);\n\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), 50 ether);\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(charlie), 50 ether);\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(bob), 0);\n    }\n\n    function test_M03_POC_IndexerBalanceTrackingCorruption() public {\n        uint256 wrapAmount = 100 ether;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), wrapAmount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, alice, uint128(wrapAmount));\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(bob, type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.recordLogs();\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, charlie, 30 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, charlie, 20 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, bob, 50 ether);\n\n        Vm.Log[] memory logs = vm.getRecordedLogs();\n        bytes32 transferEventSig = keccak256(\"Transfer(address,address,uint256)\");\n\n        int256 indexerBobBalance = 0;\n        int256 indexerAliceBalance = int256(wrapAmount);\n        int256 indexerCharlieBalance = 0;\n\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < logs.length; i++) {\n            if (logs[i].topics[0] == transferEventSig && logs[i].emitter == address(wrapper)) {\n                address from = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[1])));\n                address to = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[2])));\n                uint256 amount = abi.decode(logs[i].data, (uint256));\n\n                if (from == alice) indexerAliceBalance -= int256(amount);\n                if (from == bob) indexerBobBalance -= int256(amount);\n                if (from == charlie) indexerCharlieBalance -= int256(amount);\n\n                if (to == alice) indexerAliceBalance += int256(amount);\n                if (to == bob) indexerBobBalance += int256(amount);\n                if (to == charlie) indexerCharlieBalance += int256(amount);\n            }\n        }\n\n        uint256 actualAliceBalance = wrapper.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 actualBobBalance = wrapper.balanceOf(bob);\n        uint256 actualCharlieBalance = wrapper.balanceOf(charlie);\n\n        assertEq(actualAliceBalance, 0);\n        assertEq(actualBobBalance, 50 ether);\n        assertEq(actualCharlieBalance, 50 ether);\n\n        assertEq(indexerAliceBalance, int256(wrapAmount));\n        assertEq(indexerBobBalance, -50 ether);\n        assertEq(indexerCharlieBalance, 50 ether);\n\n        assertTrue(indexerAliceBalance != int256(actualAliceBalance));\n        assertTrue(indexerBobBalance != int256(actualBobBalance));\n    }\n\n    function test_M03_POC_ERC20StandardViolation() public {\n        uint256 wrapAmount = 100 ether;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), wrapAmount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, alice, uint128(wrapAmount));\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(bob, 50 ether);\n\n        vm.recordLogs();\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, charlie, 50 ether);\n\n        Vm.Log[] memory logs = vm.getRecordedLogs();\n        bytes32 transferEventSig = keccak256(\"Transfer(address,address,uint256)\");\n\n        address emittedFrom;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < logs.length; i++) {\n            if (logs[i].topics[0] == transferEventSig && logs[i].emitter == address(wrapper)) {\n                emittedFrom = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[1])));\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        assertTrue(emittedFrom == bob);\n        assertTrue(emittedFrom != alice);\n    }\n\n    function test_M03_POC_TransferEmitsCorrectFromAddress() public {\n        uint256 wrapAmount = 100 ether;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), wrapAmount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, alice, uint128(wrapAmount));\n\n        vm.recordLogs();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.transfer(charlie, 50 ether);\n\n        Vm.Log[] memory logs = vm.getRecordedLogs();\n        bytes32 transferEventSig = keccak256(\"Transfer(address,address,uint256)\");\n\n        address emittedFrom;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < logs.length; i++) {\n            if (logs[i].topics[0] == transferEventSig && logs[i].emitter == address(wrapper)) {\n                emittedFrom = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[1])));\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        assertEq(emittedFrom, alice);\n    }\n}\n\n```",
